# gyld-app.glade — the Gyld decision-stream app, declared as DATA (GDL-037/038).
#
# A SEPARATE app declaration rather than a growing grazel-app.glade (owner ruling
# O5, GyldGrythPlugins.md section 8). grazel loads it as a SECOND `--app` file
# when its gyld leg is switched on with `--gyld-supplier-bin`; the glade node has
# always accepted `--app` more than once, so grazel-app.glade stays exactly as it
# is, byte-identical in both of its homes.
#
# Like every app file this one is LOADED, never compiled: each declaration
# registers as an ordinary home-share record under the registrant's chain, and
# each ACL seed COMPILES TO a CapabilityGrant record at registration. The fold
# stays the only runtime authority — a runtime revocation beats a re-registered
# seed, always.
glade-app v0
app gyld

# binding <glade_id> <shape> <authority> <zone> <retention>
# The surfaces the glade-gyld supplier publishes onto after a successful build
# (GyldGrythPlugins.md 4.7, step 4.2). Pre-declared here so they exist node-side
# whether or not a supplier is running.
#
#   gyld.streams    the build's streams.json, unkeyed
#   gyld.stream     keyed by stream id: that stream's stream.json
#   gyld.decisions  keyed by stream id: that stream's decide-now.json
#   gyld.lens       keyed by <stream>/<perspective>: a {path, digest, bytes}
#                   pointer, because a lens file is fetched over HTTP from
#                   grazel's static path rather than folded onto a share
#   gyld.file       keyed by <stream>/<file>: the same kind of pointer, for
#                   that stream's projection.json (the records) and
#                   validation.json. Without it a glade root can read no
#                   record at all — the build directory had to be added as a
#                   static root by hand and re-pointed after every build.
#   gyld.output     a run's stdout and stderr lines, keyed by run id
binding gyld.streams   value share commons latest
binding gyld.stream    value share commons latest
binding gyld.decisions value share commons latest
binding gyld.lens      value share commons latest
binding gyld.file      value share commons latest
binding gyld.output    log   share commons from-cursor

# service <name> <exchange-glade-id>
# The authority provider grazel attaches, and the DIRECTED surface it answers.
# Exchanges never fan out: only the claim-holding node's provider replies.
service glade-gyld gyld.ops

# seed <principal> <share> <verb[,verb...]>
# Bootstrap shortcuts, not a parallel ACL system: compiled to CapabilityGrant
# records at registration; ordinary fold rules (revocation wins) from then on.
# The share named here is the workspace share these surfaces live on.
seed owner ws-razel read.*
seed owner ws-razel gyld.*

# workspace <share> <name>
# The same workspace share grazel-app.glade declares. Registration is idempotent
# by diff, so loading both files registers this entry once; declaring it here
# keeps this file loadable on its own.
workspace ws-razel razel
